                           List essential responsibilities for a standalone orchestration core

                           Standalone orchestration cores in hybrid AI systems like ZacAi's Heart handle critical tasks independently, ensuring reliability without external dependencies.

                           ## Goal Interpretation
                           Convert raw prompts or system events into structured goals with objectives, constraints, timelines, and success metrics. This enables planning even in offline mode using internal reasoning.

                           ## Planning and Decomposition
                           Generate hierarchical, multi-step plans identifying required actions, dependencies, and resource needs. Select optimal orchestration patterns like sequential, parallel, or hierarchical delegation.

                           ## Execution Management
                           Orchestrate task execution by routing to available modules, tools, or agents while managing retries, timeouts, fallbacks, and dynamic replanning when failures occur.

                           ## System Monitoring
                           Continuously ingest telemetry, logs, metrics, and health signals to maintain real-time awareness of component states, performance, and anomalies across the stack.

                           ## Self-Diagnostics
                           Perform root cause analysis on detected issues using pattern matching, log correlation, and reasoning over system topology to identify failures or degradation.

                           ## Self-Healing Actions
                           Execute predefined remediation playbooks such as restarts, rollbacks, scaling, circuit breaking, or graceful degradation to restore system health autonomously.

                           ## State Management
                           Maintain persistent context including conversation history, active plans, system topology, configuration state, and episodic memory of past incidents and resolutions.

                           ## Safety and Policy Enforcement
                           Apply guardrails for action authorization, risk assessment, resource limits, and ethical constraints before executing any system-impacting operations or tool calls.

                           ## Response Synthesis
                           Aggregate results from executed steps into coherent outputs, including user-facing responses, internal logs, and updated system status summaries.

                           ## Offline Fallback Reasoning
                           When modules are unavailable, simulate actions, provide diagnostic guidance, and generate hypothetical remediation steps using embedded system knowledge and virtual tooling.


